  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "16f109f5-ebf4-4796-b9ba-92af989b4e91",
    "name": "JenaValve Site API (WordPress REST) Authors API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "Derived, third-party OpenAPI description of the anonymously readable portion of the WordPress REST API served by the JenaValve corporate site at https://jenavalve.com/wp-json. JenaValve Technology publishes no developer API programme, no portal, no documentation and no keys; this is an incidental surface exposed by the site's CMS, described here because it is a real, machine-readable, publicly reachable contract.\nEvery operation below was individually probed anonymously on 2026-08-04 and returned HTTP 200. Routes that returned 401/403 anonymously (wp/v2/settings, wp/v2/block-types, wp/v2/menu-items, cky/v1/*, contact-form-7/v1/*, wp-site-health/v1/*, wp-abilities/v1/abilities) are deliberately NOT described here — see conformance/ and authentication/ for the full access-posture record. Write methods are not described: the surface answers `Allow: GET` anonymously and no write was ever attempted.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: JenaValve Technology",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
